{:paths ["src" "test"]
 ;; Rank 3: the front ends (new-app.md, landing 5). A module here may require
 ;; `app` (2) and the component backends (`tui`, `tk`, `hikap`) but never
 ;; `agent` (4). The TUI and its interactive cluster moved here at 5l-iii, so
 ;; this is kmet2's TUI in full: the widgets and selectors, the interactive
 ;; mode (`kmet.ui.tui.interactive`), the mode row and terminal `:ui` provider
 ;; (`kmet.ui.tui`), and the config command. The interactive cluster owns a run
 ;; and therefore drives the session driver; every widget reads the engine value
 ;; (`kmet.app.session.runtime`) and never the machinery that starts work (the
 ;; layer guard's `:ui` rule holds that split, and skips the cluster's files by
 ;; path).
 ;;
 ;; `kmet.agent.ui.tui.tool-renderers` keeps its namespace: shipped extensions
 ;; require it and the loader whitelist admits it by name, so the file moves and
 ;; the name does not (the two-axes rule, and the one rename a `sed` may not do).
 ;;
 ;; The moved files are `kmet.ui.*`: a new prefix for kmet2's code, so a kmet1
 ;; and a kmet2 namespace can never shadow each other on one classpath.
 :deps {kmet/reakt {:local/root "../reakt"}
        kmet/hikap {:local/root "../hikap"}
        kmet/libs {:local/root "../libs"}
        kmet/tui {:local/root "../tui"}
        kmet/ai {:local/root "../ai"}
        kmet/app {:local/root "../app"}
        kmet/srce {:local/root "../srce"}
        babashka/fs {:mvn/version "0.5.34"}
        babashka/process {:mvn/version "0.6.25"}}}
